in the history of animation which dates  back to the earliest years of film  itself there are two figures whose  contributions to our artform place them  above all others  the first is Walt Disney the second is  Hayao Miyazaki  in Japan Miyazaki Nissan is considered a  national treasure unquestionably the  most respected and important figure in  Japanese cinema today four of his films  ranked among the top 10 highest-grossing  feature films of all time in Japan  that's not just animated films but all  films which includes the Academy  award-winning spirited way the highest  grossing film of all time of Japan but  it's not the success that has so  profoundly affected animators filmmakers  and audiences around the world  it's the artistry of his films that has  I feel extremely lucky to have been  living and working during these Miyazaki  sons career to have been able to watch  and learn from his films as they have  been released they have moved me they  have inspired me and they have helped  shape me as a filmmaker in 1979 I just  graduated from Cal arts and was working  as an animator at the Disney Studios and  what I and my fellow Cal arts grads had  found was that the entire movie  moviemaking industry all of the studio's  even Disney had fallen into the belief  that animation was just for children my  peers and I tried to convince our bosses  that this wasn't true but we were shut  down at every turn this was very  discouraging to say the least  then I saw a movie from Japan that  changed my life Lupin the third castle  of Cagliostro it was Heil Miyazaki's  first film  I was totally blown away by this movie  castle of Cagliostro had adventure heart  action and humor done with such style  and sophistication and a wonderful eye  for the details of human behavior it was  proof positive as Walt Disney had shown  so many years before that animation  truly was for everyone you see I  actually was so impressed by this film  that I even wooed my wife Nancy with it  I showed her scenes from the film the  day after I met her true story it was  love at first sight it was love at first  sight but I just wanted to make sure and  thank God she loved the movie I know  that sounds really geeky but but hey 26  years and five sons later I'm proud to  say it really worked  animation is such a labor-intensive  artform every detail from a blink of an  eye to the tiniest gust of wind has to  be created painstakingly planned and  then crafted by hand frame by frame an  animated feature takes on average about  four years to create miyazaki Sanh has  directed eleven feature films more than  any other animation director in history  not only did he write as well as direct  those eleven movies he also drew all of  the storyboards every single drawing for  each film himself and every film he has  created is a masterpiece my neighbor  totoro Porco Rosa Porco Rosso Princess  Mononoke in spirited away to name just a  few  each film is full of ideas images in  emotions that are so immensely creative  that it's hard to conceive that one man  thought of them all  every time I watched miyazaki movie i  learned something new about the craft of  filmmaking miyazaki sun is the most  original filmmaker ever to work in our  medium an artist of incredible  sensitivity envisioned his films are  made with such heart and skill and  nobility of intent they gently and  piercingly awaken in their viewers a  passionate appreciation of the simple  and profound gifts we are given in our  lives from the beauty of the natural  world to the opportunities we have to  use our talents for the benefit of  others il Miyazaki has deeply influenced  animation for ever inspiring generations  of artists to work in our medium and  illuminating its limitless potential his  films are gifts to everyone who loves  the cinema and they would be watched and  cherished  as long as movies exist in stature in  influence in the range and quality of  his body of work there will be there  will never be another to rival him
 

